{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Say to the priests.</b> After He warned Israel to be holy, He warned the priests to guard themselves from impurity, for they are His attendants and the members of His household. And on the day the Tabernacle was erected this passage was stated, because on that very day they were needed for the service. And the passage of the ov and yide'oni was juxtaposed to the passage of 'say to the priests,' to tell you that by law one ought to stone one who inquires of an ov and yide'oni, for Israel has no need for them; rather, if you wish to inquire — 'say to the priests,' and they shall inquire for you through the Urim and Tummim. Tanḥuma." "<b>Sons of Aharon.</b> To include minors." "<b>He shall not defile himself among his people.</b> Among all Israel, who are his people."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:00.706677527Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}